[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-76189"] :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}5y{e}^{-x}\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y={e}^{x}$ for $\\,0\\le x\\le e?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)={e}^{t}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le e\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=5y{e}^{-x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}5\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415/selection/3e0a48d3948dd773457c5afd99fd4557c1375d8a117945fff90fc7679a7297e0" :answer/id #uuid "4cea0e19-33d9-58c8-9038-f6beb23ba941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415/selection/ce79e9900682c85a87c6db3cd2bba07135fdbc9e949f35db193e27f791e8b9ae" :answer/id #uuid "5ce6a25c-4abc-5006-9c67-ac5e94023a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415/selection/7178cf70918ffb43915730fa0988a1d32fea6c1ca20245012a99148f7dd61918" :answer/id #uuid "15fef846-3de1-5b77-b28a-e928d62653c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415/selection/e77856c4d673b6ad654eb9648c0b38d20e4f3cf48dbc273d44c208ca01729dea" :answer/id #uuid "6cf57cde-05a2-5bf3-818b-361e10a41885" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\int }_{1}^{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415/selection/b48a59872bd711cc28f076e16d2890987ac0ee5050c17101dd791b0dcaab67fc" :answer/id #uuid "2d630067-b2b7-549a-a5e7-33ebedfa8dd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "756470d7-6a29-59b7-8494-67363a155edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76415/selection/3e0a48d3948dd773457c5afd99fd4557c1375d8a117945fff90fc7679a7297e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-76415/selection/3e0a48d3948dd773457c5afd99fd4557c1375d8a117945fff90fc7679a7297e0" "q-76415/selection/ce79e9900682c85a87c6db3cd2bba07135fdbc9e949f35db193e27f791e8b9ae" "q-76415/selection/7178cf70918ffb43915730fa0988a1d32fea6c1ca20245012a99148f7dd61918" "q-76415/selection/e77856c4d673b6ad654eb9648c0b38d20e4f3cf48dbc273d44c208ca01729dea" "q-76415/selection/b48a59872bd711cc28f076e16d2890987ac0ee5050c17101dd791b0dcaab67fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76415" :question/id #uuid "05201083-bb4f-5259-a034-25bea0f3366d" :question/math-academy-id "q-76415" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ between the points $(1,2)$ and $(3,18)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2{t}^{2}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,2{t}^{2}⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+4t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(4t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76415/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e381c74c-43ed-5588-ba9a-4c7d4fb2caf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480/selection/904b2a553a3fb6d2aa06998d3d027ca83a36a6f12cf5ee42f008e428b289c6d0" :answer/id #uuid "8f7db476-7a47-5964-92ec-94bd2822730a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}(8\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480/selection/e5b3c6aaa34346cb82f0aa703702d5ceec080265b8042d8aad21405ae0a95e26" :answer/id #uuid "61e507cb-2883-5642-b828-76b8551ca0b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480/selection/be56fbfc558808b4ec5a09f48da19078c0720ec2345f2e312fac9c922e75534e" :answer/id #uuid "05d9551a-0bb5-5ff6-863b-1ace136e39e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\sqrt{2}-6\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480/selection/ffac77d44650946d80cd36c20b47bf8adbe3a4883bae818b238194dbe80724ca" :answer/id #uuid "3ea3d5e3-e01d-544f-814d-b14aed93d40f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480/selection/4b38a798b6521c3bf49abc5b92522c0eb80d86c66e3e07bb5c057b82f5360f56" :answer/id #uuid "314a4aef-6933-57af-b2ce-a3d97f5c79ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(16\\sqrt{2}-6\\sqrt{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23e4960a-1ff4-5265-aae3-3b56a8f5ebba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76480/selection/904b2a553a3fb6d2aa06998d3d027ca83a36a6f12cf5ee42f008e428b289c6d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-76480/selection/904b2a553a3fb6d2aa06998d3d027ca83a36a6f12cf5ee42f008e428b289c6d0" "q-76480/selection/e5b3c6aaa34346cb82f0aa703702d5ceec080265b8042d8aad21405ae0a95e26" "q-76480/selection/be56fbfc558808b4ec5a09f48da19078c0720ec2345f2e312fac9c922e75534e" "q-76480/selection/ffac77d44650946d80cd36c20b47bf8adbe3a4883bae818b238194dbe80724ca" "q-76480/selection/4b38a798b6521c3bf49abc5b92522c0eb80d86c66e3e07bb5c057b82f5360f56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76480" :question/id #uuid "990e94ea-023d-5851-9df0-7c57b5605a30" :question/math-academy-id "q-76480" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{1}{x},$ $\\,1\\le x\\le \\sqrt[4]{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=\\frac{1}{t}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le \\sqrt[4]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})j \\\\  & =i-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{4{(\\frac{1}{t})}^{2}}{{t}^{3}}=\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}3{x}^{5}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}$, $\\text{d}u=-\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{3/2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{2}^{3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3}}-\\sqrt{{2}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{4}-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(8\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-76480/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d261248-985f-505e-85cb-4597828f95b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76480"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199/selection/c507ed6c4d207c553876880e6b78880957b509cde347dde1b6f02e4bc7a0f86a" :answer/id #uuid "441373ef-aec4-5773-b1fb-9ca34d53726a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{t}^{3}+t-8)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199/selection/dfaa0f74b71cfdc19f098c1207bbbecca7ee15f441f96d3950c1c30a44c7e4eb" :answer/id #uuid "734edcef-4ff5-5c8c-a578-bd3b2af64a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199/selection/d43a5e8c6a3d37c460354fae23a76e5340e5569a83228c68d29200dedc2315d4" :answer/id #uuid "a972e739-468a-5bcc-8fa0-cab0fa633b86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+2t-8)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199/selection/a766fc65a70cc3e87855dec45360120be1fdcd3e1ac036825a4f8fc7064d5ec4" :answer/id #uuid "13a19305-67d3-5257-9446-de9aeede780a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(t-4)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199/selection/84de355ffe54d33598ad153de79eed4233b06e28c81a367e4268ff87227e801e" :answer/id #uuid "6ad4d858-3000-5bff-b917-1e12db16be3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}-t-4)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad41713-dc73-5809-a709-9c4f3e5db871" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-148199/selection/dfaa0f74b71cfdc19f098c1207bbbecca7ee15f441f96d3950c1c30a44c7e4eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-148199/selection/c507ed6c4d207c553876880e6b78880957b509cde347dde1b6f02e4bc7a0f86a" "q-148199/selection/dfaa0f74b71cfdc19f098c1207bbbecca7ee15f441f96d3950c1c30a44c7e4eb" "q-148199/selection/d43a5e8c6a3d37c460354fae23a76e5340e5569a83228c68d29200dedc2315d4" "q-148199/selection/a766fc65a70cc3e87855dec45360120be1fdcd3e1ac036825a4f8fc7064d5ec4" "q-148199/selection/84de355ffe54d33598ad153de79eed4233b06e28c81a367e4268ff87227e801e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-148199" :question/id #uuid "e7d9bec2-9225-5625-8a03-8734f22a69ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-148199" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-2y)\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y=2-\\frac{x}{2}$ for $\\,0\\le x\\le 2?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2-\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,2-\\frac{t}{2}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-\\frac{t}{2})j \\\\  & =i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{3}-2y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={t}^{3}-2(2-\\frac{t}{2})={t}^{3}+t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-148199/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e381c74c-43ed-5588-ba9a-4c7d4fb2caf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-148199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "2d93ff20-1e1b-5ece-b19b-b8d2d6131851" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216/selection/c1519fe0443f7c335168d712e07d2fe76542f6c5a578d93f531afd0ceeb21246" :answer/id #uuid "709f7147-b47d-5122-a184-79102b65373d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" :answer/id #uuid "242d0712-f06b-5629-bbd4-3b3d9c310f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216/selection/2c64b2f980fdf6a25e1b9157544510e71f8dad98036ed8a0c41b7b58de2d113f" :answer/id #uuid "2fe6dd4d-0594-5aff-a0c5-227124f455e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "7173092c-6f04-5a20-ac7c-dc4bf5ffb277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae993687-e497-55c3-bda5-198b267a59ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-148216/selection/c1519fe0443f7c335168d712e07d2fe76542f6c5a578d93f531afd0ceeb21246" :answer-field/choices ["q-148216/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-148216/selection/c1519fe0443f7c335168d712e07d2fe76542f6c5a578d93f531afd0ceeb21246" "q-148216/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" "q-148216/selection/2c64b2f980fdf6a25e1b9157544510e71f8dad98036ed8a0c41b7b58de2d113f" "q-148216/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-148216" :question/id #uuid "b7886d41-4806-56c1-89bc-cb400226a219" :question/math-academy-id "q-148216" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+y$ along the line $y=x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =i+\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t+t=2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{t}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-148216/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d261248-985f-505e-85cb-4597828f95b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-148216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
